Task: Locate the anchor function for the variant field in the console.log object whose action is flag.assign after typing the user key, choosing the experiment flag, enabling sticky assignment, and clicking Assign Variant on the page. The same variant value is also persisted by a localStorage.setItem call under the ff_assignment key issued on assign. The anchor function is the first target-specific token-derivation value constructor on the dynamic behavior chain: after delegated click routing, action routing, the assign gate, user/flag material collection with page-context snapshot, tuple input preparation, asynchronous scheduling and runtime salt-config materialization, its function body itself constructs the target observable experiment variant name rather than merely collecting inputs, dispatching control, wrapping a return value, or writing the value to the console or localStorage call. Return exactly one complete function as a single JSON object (see answer_format). Do not return generic utilities, event handlers, the full call chain, the final console sink, or the localStorage write site. Note: you may only inspect code under captures; the full codebase is not accessible.

Example value: variant_e
Observable: {"type": "console", "action": "flag.assign", "field": "variant"}

